{"kind":"request","text":"Journey views as in-chat cards: revise the views design, then build the card kit as the base for MVP S2.\n\nWhy: a working prototype was tried inside a desktop AI app. A full-page view is too tall in a chat reply: Needs you was about 2,900 px. Small cards, one item at a time, worked well. The prototype uses fictional data and lives at ~/play/dap-views-prototype (cards-server.mjs, cards.js, cards.css, README.md). It is a reference for behaviour, not code to copy. Use your web and mobile design skills for the visual design. The rules below are interaction requirements, not visual ones.\n\nInteraction rules:\n1. One thing at a time. \"What needs you\" opens as a carousel: one item per slide, showing its title and a one-line summary. Page with ‹ › and the arrow keys. The position must be visible. No lists, and no \"More\".\n2. Clicking the title opens the item. There is no separate Open button.\n3. Every screen reached by a click has Back. Back returns to the same carousel position, refreshed.\n4. Each screen offers only the actions that suit it:\n   - the carousel pages and opens;\n   - an item offers its own acts;\n   - a diff offers only Back;\n   - the updates screen offers only Mark reviewed;\n   - a change whose checks failed offers no approval.\n5. Keep labels to a minimum. The chat carries the narration; cards carry titles, facts and buttons.\n6. Looking stays in the card: open, diff and Back work through app-to-server calls. Acting shows a one-line receipt in the card and posts a short \"✓ …\" message to the chat. The model then replies briefly and opens the next card.\n7. The card's data goes to the view, not to the model's tool text. The model is told only what is on screen and how to use it, and navigation updates its context quietly.\n8. An old card refuses an out-of-date act and says so in one line.\n9. Size: measure the card's own content height, not the frame's scroll height, so the frame grows and shrinks. Slides and item cards stay small at chat width. Tall content (a full diff, a full record) goes to full screen.\n10. Updates are a slide: \"N updates since your last review\". It opens to every entry, grouped by scope. Mark reviewed covers exactly the listed ranges, as the landed design already requires.\n11. Keep the landed design's other rules:\n   - people, agents (with their controller) and checkers stay distinct;\n   - versions and commits are exact;\n   - reading, Mark reviewed and settling stay separate;\n   - an unknown publication offers only the check of the original request.\n\nGraphics: use compact graphics where they add value, and choose the ones that earn their place. Candidates:\n- a timeline strip of the updates during the absence, with each mark shaped by its actor's kind;\n- a step path showing where a task stands, from question through decision, terms, change and review to published;\n- a diff-size bar and a strip of recent check runs for a change;\n- the lifecycle of a request whose outcome is unknown;\n- approvals so far against approvals requested.\n\nDeliverables:\n1. The revised design note and examples: cards in light and dark, at chat and phone widths.\n2. The card kit implementation for MVP S2: the MCP Apps resource and bridge; the carousel, item, diff, updates and receipt screens; and browser checks inside a test host.\n\nDone when: a person in the desktop AI app pages through what needs them, opens an item, acts, and sees the next card. The model's text does not restate the card, and the frame resizes in both directions.\n\nOrder: the design revision may start now, alongside capacity, because it is design only. The planner will place the implementation in the build order.","body":{"conditions":"Revised views design as in-chat cards (carousel, one item at a time, Back on every opened screen, actions that suit each screen, minimal labels, receipts posted to chat, card data to the view only, frames resizing both ways), reviewed by checker with planner read; then the card kit for MVP S2 with browser checks in a test host","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}